# AC 9 and AC 10, in one session, on a real clock.
#
# qwen3.5:9b thinks for ninety seconds or more before it says anything, which is
# the awkward fact that makes this row easy: any turn at all straddles a minute
# boundary, so a `*/1 * * * *` job is guaranteed to come due mid-turn. The only
# thing being arranged below is *when* the turn starts, so the boundary lands
# well inside it rather than at either edge.

wait: 8
send: Schedule a prompt to run every minute that asks what time it is.

# Long enough for the turn to finish AND for one whole minute to pass with the
# session sitting at an idle prompt. That stretch is AC 9.
wait: 190
mark: === AC 9 above: nothing was typed, so anything up there fired on its own ===

# Start the long turn a quarter of a minute in, so :00 arrives with the reply
# part written and the model still generating.
at-second: 25
send: Write a detailed 400 word explanation of how a mechanical clock escapement works. Do not use any tools.
idle: 170
mark: === AC 10 above: did a scheduled turn cut into that reply, or wait for it? ===

idle: 70
send: /exit
